# Generated artifacts — never 3-way merged.
#
# `dashboard.html` conflicted on three consecutive merges with main, and the
# resolution was identical every time: throw both sides away and rerun the
# generator. A conflict in a projection is not a decision — there is nothing in
# either side that the sources do not already contain.
#
# `merge=keep-ours` resolves these to our side and exits clean; the pre-commit
# hook's staleness check then forces a regenerate before the commit lands, so
# "ours" is never what ships. `scripts/hooks/install.sh` registers the driver.
#
# These stay committed rather than ignored: the dashboard is the founder-facing
# artifact and is opened from a fresh clone without running Python.

reports/*/dashboard.html   merge=keep-ours linguist-generated=true
reports/*/BRIEF.md         merge=keep-ours linguist-generated=true
